1
00:00:00,393 --> 00:00:04,840
Isn’t it amazing?
Our bakery has grown so big!

2
00:00:04,865 --> 00:00:06,264
Just look at it! See…

3
00:00:06,289 --> 00:00:07,813
Ah, correction! Bake shop—

4
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:10,463
because no one has to
stand while eating anymore,

5
00:00:10,602 --> 00:00:14,402
we can now accommodate
so many customers, right?

6
00:00:14,427 --> 00:00:18,572
And that’s not all! We have visitors
tonight, all the way from Tagaytay!

7
00:00:18,597 --> 00:00:21,435
Say hi to the vlog! Is the food good?

8
00:00:21,715 --> 00:00:23,741
- Yes, yes, the best!
- Delicious! Cheers!

9
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:24,615
Super good, right?

10
00:00:25,118 --> 00:00:27,418
Scrumptious! Absolutely the best!

11
00:00:27,443 --> 00:00:29,873
You know what, guys, here’s the thing…

12
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:31,444
Huh? What do you mean "here’s the thing"?

13
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:32,911
There’s more?

14
00:00:32,936 --> 00:00:38,417
Yes, Kuya! Guys, stay tuned for the
newest additions to our menu—short orders!

15
00:00:38,805 --> 00:00:41,673
Only here at Bake Haus of U…

16
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:43,707
Bake… Shop!

17
00:00:45,288 --> 00:00:48,195
That was awesome,
Kuya! That’s gonna be a hit!

18
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,522
Nice, nice, nice, nice!

19
00:00:50,718 --> 00:00:52,224
You’re still editing the intro, right?

20
00:00:52,249 --> 00:00:54,708
Hey, Tash, Andres,
where should we put this?

21
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:55,181
Hold on…

22
00:00:55,206 --> 00:00:58,909
Oh, just put it at the house. We still
need to sort the short orders, right?

23
00:00:59,048 --> 00:01:00,110
Wait, wait.

24
00:01:00,135 --> 00:01:01,165
Why?

25
00:01:02,112 --> 00:01:03,202
That’s wilted already!

26
00:01:03,227 --> 00:01:04,600
Remember this, Tash?

27
00:01:04,625 --> 00:01:05,785
The rose that—

28
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:08,450
Bup, bup, bup, bup! Tash, no spoilers!

29
00:01:08,723 --> 00:01:11,270
They don’t know what
happened at the debut yet, right?

30
00:01:11,805 --> 00:01:12,383
Debut?

31
00:01:12,408 --> 00:01:16,068
You’re talking about spoilers, but
you just mentioned the debut yourself.

32
00:01:17,185 --> 00:01:18,938
Okay, okay, my bad. Anyway!

33
00:01:18,993 --> 00:01:23,610
Let’s all just sit back, relax, and enjoy
this episode full of family love, okay?

34
00:01:24,348 --> 00:01:26,601
Oh, you have a point there.

35
00:01:29,182 --> 00:01:30,608
Look… they’re dancing.

36
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:39,567
Wow! Now that’s a breakfast worth having!

37
00:02:39,592 --> 00:02:40,200
Full?

38
00:02:40,225 --> 00:02:41,547
The best! So full!

39
00:02:42,866 --> 00:02:43,930
- My love…
- Mmm?

40
00:02:44,001 --> 00:02:45,121
You really have a way with cooking.

41
00:02:51,908 --> 00:02:52,931
Wow!

42
00:02:55,923 --> 00:02:58,189
Lola Maxi’s in a great mood today!

43
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:00,488
Of course!

44
00:03:00,663 --> 00:03:04,029
My grandkids’ birthday is coming up!

45
00:03:04,054 --> 00:03:06,022
Oh, that’s right!

46
00:03:06,047 --> 00:03:09,778
So, what’s the plan for your
birthday, Atasha, Andres?

47
00:03:09,803 --> 00:03:11,496
Oh, we can skip mine.
Let’s focus on Tash.

48
00:03:11,543 --> 00:03:12,624
Whoa!

49
00:03:12,649 --> 00:03:13,880
You’re skipping your birthday?

50
00:03:13,905 --> 00:03:21,077
But… why don’t we just
keep it simple, like always?

51
00:03:21,378 --> 00:03:24,880
Andres, Atasha, your birthdays have
always been celebrated together—it’s fun,

52
00:03:25,995 --> 00:03:28,455
and we save money. Right?

53
00:03:28,797 --> 00:03:30,638
- Right, right.
- Dad, you’re right. You’re totally right.

54
00:03:30,663 --> 00:03:31,017
See?!

55
00:03:31,042 --> 00:03:36,047
Yeah, and what’s really important is
that our family is complete and healthy,

56
00:03:36,624 --> 00:03:38,251
whether there’s
a party or not.

57
00:03:39,478 --> 00:03:41,365
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

58
00:03:41,582 --> 00:03:44,109
No way! That’s not okay!

59
00:03:44,841 --> 00:03:50,926
Tash, how many years have your
parents promised to throw you a debut?

60
00:03:51,197 --> 00:03:53,497
Every year, it never happens!

61
00:03:53,522 --> 00:03:55,785
And now, it’s not
happening again?! No way!

62
00:03:56,029 --> 00:03:59,989
Lola, it’s really okay.
I’m turning 23 anyway.

63
00:04:00,299 --> 00:04:01,252
That’s exactly my point!

64
00:04:01,463 --> 00:04:04,976
You’re turning 23! Your
debut is five years overdue!

65
00:04:05,422 --> 00:04:09,674
No way, Tash. It has to happen this year!

66
00:04:09,947 --> 00:04:12,914
Lola Maxi, debuts are expensive.

67
00:04:13,075 --> 00:04:13,802
I don’t care!

68
00:04:14,468 --> 00:04:18,425
I’ll be so disappointed if this
debut doesn’t push through this year!

69
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:20,811
It’s important to me that my
granddaughter has her debut!

70
00:04:21,330 --> 00:04:24,070
Lola Maxi, please, please sit down first.

71
00:04:28,258 --> 00:04:29,505
Okay, okay, I got it…

72
00:04:40,788 --> 00:04:41,856
Lola Maxi,

73
00:04:43,746 --> 00:04:47,434
we can figure something out, right?

74
00:04:49,352 --> 00:04:51,457
And where do you plan to get the money?

75
00:05:00,812 --> 00:05:01,618
Ahem…

76
00:05:01,643 --> 00:05:02,700
- Huh?!
- Oh?

77
00:05:03,822 --> 00:05:04,981
- Oh?
- Oooh!

78
00:05:08,591 --> 00:05:11,698
Life is really quite simple.

79
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:16,495
Oh, Tash! You’re getting a debut!

80
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,906
Oh my gosh, thank you! Thank you!

81
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:21,754
See?

82
00:05:24,473 --> 00:05:29,492
Tso K, when are you finally
joining my Zumba sessions?

83
00:05:32,193 --> 00:05:35,080
Whooo, whooo, it’s so hot!

84
00:05:35,571 --> 00:05:41,031
But you know, Tso K, I can give
you private Zumba sessions inside.

85
00:05:41,653 --> 00:05:43,308
- Huh?!
- It’s possible, inside!

86
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:44,243
- Oh no!
- Ye–

87
00:05:44,268 --> 00:05:47,322
Hey, Mariposa! Can you just stop?

88
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:49,988
I told you to leave me alone,
but you keep doing this to me!

89
00:05:50,179 --> 00:05:55,244
You’re always walking around like that—I
don’t know if your neck is broken or what…

90
00:05:55,269 --> 00:05:56,655
Now I look like a dinosaur…

91
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:59,376
Right? What is that? Just stop, will you?!

92
00:06:00,156 --> 00:06:02,346
- Looks like someone’s in a bad mood today!
- Do I really look like a dinosaur?

93
00:06:02,791 --> 00:06:04,597
- Oh?
- Hi, Tash!

94
00:06:04,688 --> 00:06:06,261
Tash, are you okay?

95
00:06:07,803 --> 00:06:09,303
It’s just… Lola.

96
00:06:09,757 --> 00:06:13,041
Our birthday was supposed
to be a simple celebration,

97
00:06:13,381 --> 00:06:15,809
but now she wants me to have a debut.

98
00:06:16,489 --> 00:06:18,683
- You’re having a debut?!
- Debut?!

99
00:06:18,719 --> 00:06:20,273
I’m so excited!

100
00:06:20,696 --> 00:06:24,463
Tash, that’s such an important
milestone for us women!

101
00:06:24,488 --> 00:06:26,089
Correct, correct, correct, correct!

102
00:06:26,114 --> 00:06:27,625
- That’s huge!
- Right?! I was so shocked!

103
00:06:27,650 --> 00:06:28,526
Exciting!

104
00:06:28,551 --> 00:06:30,396
Oh, but why do you look sad?

105
00:06:30,421 --> 00:06:34,520
Yeah, you all have a point,
but it’s just too expensive.

106
00:06:35,828 --> 00:06:40,180
I don’t want to spend too much.
Honestly, I’d be fine without it.

107
00:06:40,503 --> 00:06:46,090
Actually, I have a cousin
who’s an event coordinator!

108
00:06:46,115 --> 00:06:49,459
Oh! She’s great at budgeting for debuts!

109
00:06:49,484 --> 00:06:50,872
- Bup-bup!
- Wow! Really?!

110
00:06:50,897 --> 00:06:53,805
Wait a second, I just heard something!

111
00:06:54,151 --> 00:06:56,031
Another debut talk?

112
00:06:56,555 --> 00:07:00,395
This is why you’re always short on
money—you keep thinking about spending!

113
00:07:00,902 --> 00:07:05,409
Debuts aren’t something you should
be wasting money on! What a waste!

114
00:07:06,037 --> 00:07:06,858
Money!

115
00:07:06,883 --> 00:07:08,475
Money, money, money, money, money!

116
00:07:08,817 --> 00:07:11,544
Tso K, aren’t you tired of
always talking about money?

117
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,131
Are you tired?

118
00:07:14,195 --> 00:07:16,688
Well, what if I get tired of
letting you stay in my house?

119
00:07:16,721 --> 00:07:18,824
- Oh, we’re staying quiet…
- Huh?! I’m getting tired too!

120
00:07:19,528 --> 00:07:21,548
- Come on, Tso K…
- Oh no!

121
00:07:21,573 --> 00:07:25,387
You know I’m just joking…
every now and then!

122
00:07:25,705 --> 00:07:26,622
You’re unbelievable!

123
00:07:26,647 --> 00:07:28,355
So, Tash? No debut for you?

124
00:07:29,452 --> 00:07:31,757
- Sure, no problem, Tso K.
- Well, that’s a little mean, Tso K…

125
00:07:31,782 --> 00:07:34,155
You know how he is… money,
money, money, money, money, money…

126
00:07:36,501 --> 00:07:37,094
That looks great!

127
00:07:37,119 --> 00:07:39,452
Dad, look at these beautiful debut gowns!

128
00:07:39,965 --> 00:07:40,805
- Andres!
- What?

129
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:44,976
Those are the kind of gowns
your future wife should be wearing!

130
00:07:45,001 --> 00:07:45,649
Huh?!

131
00:07:45,674 --> 00:07:46,607
What? Wife?!

132
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:48,271
We’re talking about
weddings already, my love?!

133
00:07:48,533 --> 00:07:53,052
What I’m saying is, just look at the
prices of these gowns—100,000 pesos!

134
00:07:53,077 --> 00:07:53,532
Huh?!

135
00:07:53,557 --> 00:07:56,821
- Yeah, a hundred thousand!
- Oh no, oh no! Look, listen up!

136
00:07:56,846 --> 00:08:00,303
Look at this—the venue,
catering, 700,000 pesos!

137
00:08:00,627 --> 00:08:02,179
Whoa, that’s insanely expensive!

138
00:08:02,204 --> 00:08:06,444
See? Even our supplies
here are so pricey.

139
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:10,218
If that’s the case…
then let’s just not go

140
00:08:10,243 --> 00:08:13,738
through with it. We don’t
have that kind of money.

141
00:08:15,058 --> 00:08:16,605
It’s not that… it’s not that—

142
00:08:17,505 --> 00:08:18,098
- Okay…
- Tash…

143
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,657
Guys, I want you to meet Ate Elle,

144
00:08:20,696 --> 00:08:28,368
cousin of Ate Mariposa, and she’s the
key to making Lola’s dream debut happen.

145
00:08:28,463 --> 00:08:30,137
Oh! Hi, Elle!

146
00:08:30,162 --> 00:08:31,989
- Hello, hello, hi!
- Hello!

147
00:08:32,598 --> 00:08:36,077
Wait a minute, you got a coordinator?

148
00:08:36,504 --> 00:08:37,017
Huh?

149
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:38,975
We’re already struggling with the budget.

150
00:08:39,175 --> 00:08:42,230
No offense, Elle, but we
really are having a hard

151
00:08:42,254 --> 00:08:45,999
time with expenses—venue,
gown, hundreds of thousands!

152
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:49,709
That’s okay, don’t worry! I got this.

153
00:08:49,909 --> 00:08:53,775
I’m tied up with suppliers, so I can
get things through exchange deals.

154
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:54,283
Oh!

155
00:08:54,308 --> 00:08:55,616
- Ex-deal?!
- Ex-deal?!

156
00:08:56,659 --> 00:08:59,059
Yes, ex-deal!

157
00:08:59,172 --> 00:09:01,032
Okay, okay… explain, explain.

158
00:09:01,057 --> 00:09:02,200
- Like your bake shop…
- Go on…

159
00:09:02,225 --> 00:09:06,825
So, we can find suppliers who
are open to exchange deals.

160
00:09:06,850 --> 00:09:11,367
They provide what we need,
and when they need something, we

161
00:09:11,391 --> 00:09:15,907
provide it—like your bake shop
can offer cakes and pastries.

162
00:09:15,932 --> 00:09:17,123
Ah, excuse me?

163
00:09:17,269 --> 00:09:18,280
Ate Elle?

164
00:09:18,533 --> 00:09:21,729
Look at me—I’m the mom!

165
00:09:21,754 --> 00:09:23,288
Daddy, Daddy!

166
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,967
I’m Atasha’s mom, right?

167
00:09:25,992 --> 00:09:28,092
But I get what you’re saying!

168
00:09:28,243 --> 00:09:31,876
If we do an exchange
deal, we provide the cakes.

169
00:09:31,936 --> 00:09:32,830
Is that correct?

170
00:09:32,855 --> 00:09:33,968
That’s right, Ma’am!

171
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:35,455
Look at me when you talk, okay?

172
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,796
This will really help us save a lot.

173
00:09:37,821 --> 00:09:40,453
Oh, really? That’s great,
that’s great, that’s great!

174
00:09:40,478 --> 00:09:41,903
See? It’s possible after all!

175
00:09:44,655 --> 00:09:48,775
But wait, what about Lola
Maxi? She already said no.

176
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:52,079
Didn’t you hear what Elle said?
She’ll find a way!

177
00:09:52,104 --> 00:10:00,783
Oh my! My dream debut for my
granddaughter is really happening!

178
00:10:04,621 --> 00:10:06,962
Wow, that’s a lot—five tho—can
you even pay five thousand?

179
00:10:06,987 --> 00:10:08,150
Crazy!

180
00:10:09,329 --> 00:10:10,382
This is all I can give you!

181
00:10:10,407 --> 00:10:13,883
Is that really how much
debut parties cost now?

182
00:10:13,908 --> 00:10:15,112
Mm-hmm! Expensive, right?

183
00:10:15,137 --> 00:10:16,279
Oh, that’s not all!

184
00:10:16,304 --> 00:10:19,604
You also have to pay for
the food and all the effort!

185
00:10:20,066 --> 00:10:21,885
Venue, ten K.

186
00:10:22,058 --> 00:10:23,505
Ten K? Check!

187
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:25,211
Caterer, ten K.

188
00:10:25,308 --> 00:10:26,748
Ten K, check!

189
00:10:27,343 --> 00:10:28,830
Gown and decor, five K!

190
00:10:29,278 --> 00:10:30,865
Five K, check!

191
00:10:31,044 --> 00:10:32,978
Sounds and light, five K.

192
00:10:33,364 --> 00:10:34,977
Five K, check!

193
00:10:35,002 --> 00:10:36,109
Crew, five K!

194
00:10:36,403 --> 00:10:38,070
Five K, check!

195
00:10:38,509 --> 00:10:40,230
Cousin, how much is that in total?

196
00:10:40,255 --> 00:10:44,961
Uh, five, six, seven, eight, ni—

197
00:10:45,823 --> 00:10:48,876
Cous! What are you doing?
Next question, please!

198
00:10:48,901 --> 00:10:53,514
You know, Mariposa, good
thing you’re pretty, huh?

199
00:10:53,539 --> 00:10:57,046
Oh my god, cousin! Mm, wait,
how much did they give you?

200
00:10:57,693 --> 00:10:59,726
Oh, Cous, nothing.

201
00:10:59,751 --> 00:11:01,578
What?! Everything’s ex-deal?!

202
00:11:01,859 --> 00:11:04,739
You know what, let’s just cancel
some of these. Cut out the—

203
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:06,345
Wait, wait, wait…

204
00:11:06,644 --> 00:11:10,931
let’s not, or Lola might get
mad if the debut turns out bad.

205
00:11:11,067 --> 00:11:14,444
See? That’s what I’m talking about!

206
00:11:14,702 --> 00:11:17,609
You’re planning this big party,
but you don’t even have money!

207
00:11:18,195 --> 00:11:19,234
Now what?

208
00:11:19,999 --> 00:11:21,199
- Three?
- Yes.

209
00:11:21,224 --> 00:11:23,031
- Alright, here’s what we’ll do.
- Mm, mm?

210
00:11:23,056 --> 00:11:25,256
I’ll take care of cooking
the food… alright?

211
00:11:25,281 --> 00:11:27,562
And then you guys can be the crew, right?

212
00:11:27,587 --> 00:11:28,270
- Yes!
- Yes!

213
00:11:28,295 --> 00:11:29,789
- Right? That works?
- We’ll help you.

214
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,683
Assistant chef, assistant chef.

215
00:11:31,708 --> 00:11:32,980
- Yes!
- That works!

216
00:11:33,034 --> 00:11:34,812
The three of us are chefs now!

217
00:11:40,175 --> 00:11:41,548
Uh, excuse me?

218
00:11:41,855 --> 00:11:45,200
Atasha, why do you look so stressed again?

219
00:11:45,478 --> 00:11:47,665
Ugh, nothing fits me.

220
00:11:47,986 --> 00:11:50,733
The last gown I wore was from my JS Prom!

221
00:11:51,036 --> 00:11:53,183
Atasha, just relax!

222
00:11:53,436 --> 00:11:56,984
Who knows? Elle might be
able to get an ex-deal for that too.

223
00:11:57,532 --> 00:11:59,585
Maybe we should just back out?

224
00:12:00,705 --> 00:12:01,732
Tash,

225
00:12:02,426 --> 00:12:03,437
you know,

226
00:12:04,999 --> 00:12:11,095
I just wanted you to experience
what I never got to experience.

227
00:12:11,728 --> 00:12:17,597
But if you really don’t want to, it’s
okay. We don’t have to go through with it.

228
00:12:19,586 --> 00:12:20,595
Okay.

229
00:12:22,070 --> 00:12:25,504
- Hello!
- Hello, hello, hello!

230
00:12:25,529 --> 00:12:28,141
Are you guys ready for food tasting?!

231
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:30,212
- Wow!
- Wow!

232
00:12:30,706 --> 00:12:35,793
Dad, I told Ate Elle that
I’ll handle the cooking…

233
00:12:35,818 --> 00:12:36,375
Okay…?

234
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,373
- …so we can save money, right?
- That’s right!

235
00:12:38,398 --> 00:12:39,958
Wow!

236
00:12:39,983 --> 00:12:42,088
Really, bro? Thank you.

237
00:12:42,113 --> 00:12:44,419
So what are we waiting for?
Come on, come on!

238
00:12:47,053 --> 00:12:48,627
Smells good!

239
00:12:50,714 --> 00:12:52,228
Atasha, you have the honors!

240
00:12:52,647 --> 00:12:55,727
- Wow!
- Magic!

241
00:12:55,752 --> 00:13:01,080
Wow, so… right here, we have
seafood delight that is slowly boiled,

242
00:13:01,611 --> 00:13:03,431
made out of sea bass.

243
00:13:03,456 --> 00:13:09,915
We have slow-cooked pork
braised in sauce, and orange octopus.

244
00:13:09,970 --> 00:13:11,797
Orange Octopus?!

245
00:13:12,116 --> 00:13:17,016
That’s just fish balls, squid balls, and
barbecue. You just made it sound fancy.

246
00:13:19,205 --> 00:13:21,985
No, I didn’t. Look, it smells amazing!

247
00:13:22,458 --> 00:13:23,592
Taste it, please, taste it.

248
00:13:23,617 --> 00:13:25,924
Why are we just talking
about it? Let’s taste it already.

249
00:13:25,949 --> 00:13:28,490
Andres made it himself!
Andres, you made this?

250
00:13:28,562 --> 00:13:29,184
Mm-hmm!

251
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,226
You cooked this?!

252
00:13:30,327 --> 00:13:31,040
Taste it!

253
00:13:31,072 --> 00:13:32,786
Mm-hmmm!
Look, I even have a bow on my apron.

254
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:37,617
You first, you first! You first
because it’s your birthday, Atasha.

255
00:13:37,642 --> 00:13:38,699
It’s good.

256
00:13:38,724 --> 00:13:39,658
Is it?

257
00:13:40,551 --> 00:13:41,791
Oh!
Guys, have you heard the news?

258
00:13:41,864 --> 00:13:42,644
- What?
- News?

259
00:13:42,669 --> 00:13:46,774
Our food is a success. At least
we’ve solved one of our problems.

260
00:13:46,799 --> 00:13:49,537
Wow, perfect!

261
00:13:50,781 --> 00:13:57,386
Don’t worry, Lola Maxi’s dream of a
grand debut for your sister will come true.

262
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:03,300
Orb, can you help me out?

263
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:06,629
I don’t know what to
do for Tash’s birthday.

264
00:14:07,529 --> 00:14:12,095
Oh my gosh, it’s so
hard to think of something!

265
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,652
Huh?!

266
00:14:12,677 --> 00:14:14,237
Mariposa, wait.

267
00:14:14,388 --> 00:14:15,926
You’re having a hard time thinking?

268
00:14:16,113 --> 00:14:18,667
Well, of course, you
are—you don’t have a brain!

269
00:14:18,692 --> 00:14:20,222
Oh yeah, you’re right!

270
00:14:20,743 --> 00:14:23,269
I didn’t think of that! Thanks!

271
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:25,004
You’re unbelievable.

272
00:14:25,333 --> 00:14:29,652
You know, Mariposa, you could give
her something useful for her debut, right?

273
00:14:29,831 --> 00:14:32,091
Oh yeah… you’re so smart, Orb!

274
00:14:32,173 --> 00:14:33,673
- Right?!
- That was a good one, Andres!

275
00:14:33,698 --> 00:14:34,040
True!

276
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:38,594
Orb, you don’t even ask me. My
birthday is tomorrow too, remember?

277
00:14:38,619 --> 00:14:40,044
Yeah, their birthdays are back-to-back.

278
00:14:40,844 --> 00:14:42,330
Come on, Orb!

279
00:14:45,618 --> 00:14:47,352
Maybe… a kiss instead?

280
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,800
Wait, a kiss?!

281
00:14:51,108 --> 00:14:53,168
Ye-yea–yeah-that works!

282
00:14:53,268 --> 00:14:54,326
Hey!

283
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:55,834
Whoa, are they really gonna kiss?!

284
00:15:04,868 --> 00:15:06,048
Hey!

285
00:15:06,073 --> 00:15:07,657
- Tso K…
- Who’s kissing?!

286
00:15:07,682 --> 00:15:09,003
What are you doing, kissing-kissing?!

287
00:15:09,028 --> 00:15:10,431
Rub your faces on the wall instead!

288
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:11,590
Just wait till I—

289
00:15:11,615 --> 00:15:12,728
- Tso K!
- You guys!

290
00:15:13,532 --> 00:15:15,377
Anne, behave yourself!

291
00:15:16,069 --> 00:15:17,689
You look like you really want that kiss!

292
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:20,739
I can see it in your eyes!
You want it?! A kiss?!

293
00:15:22,105 --> 00:15:23,185
Tso K, what’s that you’re holding?

294
00:15:23,356 --> 00:15:24,536
Is that for Tash?

295
00:15:24,561 --> 00:15:26,349
- For Tash!
- Oh really?!

296
00:15:26,374 --> 00:15:31,285
Of course! You know me, I always give Tash
something special, something she’ll love!

297
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:33,373
I don’t give cheap gifts!

298
00:15:33,444 --> 00:15:34,618
It’s expensive!

299
00:15:34,643 --> 00:15:36,644
Wow!

300
00:15:36,669 --> 00:15:38,783
Let me guess!

301
00:15:38,808 --> 00:15:39,696
Oh, just a guess, okay?

302
00:15:39,721 --> 00:15:41,290
Just by the way you’re holding it…

303
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:42,110
Go ahead, guess!

304
00:15:42,192 --> 00:15:43,879
Check it, Iskineport. Check it, check it!

305
00:15:43,904 --> 00:15:44,825
Whoa…

306
00:15:45,776 --> 00:15:46,809
- That looks fancy!
- So what is it?

307
00:15:46,834 --> 00:15:47,958
Just a guess!

308
00:15:48,226 --> 00:15:49,372
Hey!

309
00:15:49,937 --> 00:15:51,185
- Whoa!
- What?!

310
00:15:51,917 --> 00:15:55,500
I think I have an idea, but…

311
00:15:55,787 --> 00:15:56,387
Wait—

312
00:15:56,459 --> 00:15:58,119
My turn! Let me guess! Let me guess!

313
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,319
Stop shaking it!

314
00:16:00,344 --> 00:16:02,688
It feels like… umm… I
think it’s something special!

315
00:16:02,713 --> 00:16:03,555
Something special.

316
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:05,713
Anne, what are you doing?! Stop shaking it!

317
00:16:05,738 --> 00:16:07,157
- Shaking it?!
- Huh?

318
00:16:07,456 --> 00:16:09,536
- Why—
- Stop—

319
00:16:10,033 --> 00:16:11,773
Hey! Oh no!

320
00:16:12,448 --> 00:16:13,648
I can’t figure it out!

321
00:16:13,673 --> 00:16:14,721
Stop shaking it!

322
00:16:14,746 --> 00:16:17,215
It sounds like coins! Listen!

323
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:18,435
Maybe it’s coins!

324
00:16:20,043 --> 00:16:23,010
- No! It’s popcorn! Popcorn!
- Give it here!

325
00:16:23,035 --> 00:16:24,099
Popcorn!

326
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:26,352
It’s empty!

327
00:16:26,377 --> 00:16:27,489
Why is there no sound anymore?

328
00:16:27,688 --> 00:16:28,881
- No sound?
- Yes!

329
00:16:29,892 --> 00:16:31,302
Did one of you take it?

330
00:16:31,494 --> 00:16:32,512
No, it’s still in there!

331
00:16:32,537 --> 00:16:35,984
- I told you not to shake it.
- We only shook it very, very gently.

332
00:16:36,494 --> 00:16:39,414
Earlier, I said don’t shake it.

333
00:16:40,189 --> 00:16:41,335
- I—
- Oh!

334
00:16:41,748 --> 00:16:43,108
What is this, an urn?!

335
00:16:44,925 --> 00:16:46,412
With a soul inside?!

336
00:16:48,506 --> 00:16:50,166
What happened?!

337
00:16:50,191 --> 00:16:51,039
What even is your gift?!

338
00:16:51,101 --> 00:16:52,468
It’s a figurine!

339
00:16:52,493 --> 00:16:53,418
A figurine?!

340
00:16:53,443 --> 00:16:55,163
Why didn’t you say that earlier?!

341
00:16:55,188 --> 00:16:57,232
- You should’ve said so!
- You should’ve said something earlier!

342
00:16:57,379 --> 00:17:03,013
- One, two, three, four, fi–oh!
- Ouch! What was that?!

343
00:17:03,238 --> 00:17:04,678
Wow, are you okay?

344
00:17:05,148 --> 00:17:06,901
You've been in a bad
mood all day, Tash!

345
00:17:06,926 --> 00:17:10,346
Well, we keep practicing this dance,

346
00:17:10,371 --> 00:17:12,825
but I don’t even have a
gown to wear for that debut!

347
00:17:13,467 --> 00:17:19,010
And honestly, why is Lola even
throwing a debut if we can’t afford it?!

348
00:17:19,036 --> 00:17:20,205
I don’t know!

349
00:17:20,469 --> 00:17:22,569
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

350
00:17:22,841 --> 00:17:24,495
- Surprise!
- Surprise.

351
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,007
- Come on, cheer up!
- Cheer up! Yeah!

352
00:17:27,032 --> 00:17:27,998
Thank you, guys!

353
00:17:28,033 --> 00:17:29,286
Everyone heard that, you know.

354
00:17:29,650 --> 00:17:31,530
My birthday isn’t until tomorrow.

355
00:17:31,685 --> 00:17:35,751
Whatever! Here, we got
you a sash, Tash! Atashas!

356
00:17:35,776 --> 00:17:36,058
Atashas!

357
00:17:36,083 --> 00:17:40,822
Wear this tomorrow! Look, there are
gloves too, all the way up your arms.

358
00:17:40,847 --> 00:17:42,627
- That’s Iskineport!
- And there’s a crown!

359
00:17:42,652 --> 00:17:43,615
Wow, see?!

360
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,806
Come on, be happy!

361
00:17:45,195 --> 00:17:47,455
- Princess Tash!
- Princess Tash!

362
00:17:47,699 --> 00:17:48,792
Yeah, right.

363
00:17:49,618 --> 00:17:51,065
What? You don’t like it?

364
00:17:52,724 --> 00:17:54,970
- No – I really do.
- Oh?

365
00:17:54,995 --> 00:17:56,702
And I really appreciate it.

366
00:17:56,734 --> 00:17:57,833
See? You appreciate it!

367
00:17:57,922 --> 00:18:00,435
But... I still don’t have a gown.

368
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:03,625
Well, we can’t afford
that. Gowns are expensive!

369
00:18:04,204 --> 00:18:07,111
Tash, it’s okay! Everything will be fine.

370
00:18:07,895 --> 00:18:08,789
Okay?

371
00:18:08,814 --> 00:18:13,587
Tash? Here’s your ex-deal gown!

372
00:18:13,612 --> 00:18:14,833
There it is!

373
00:18:15,317 --> 00:18:18,310
- Wow! It’s beautiful!
- Now, don’t be sad anymore!

374
00:18:19,289 --> 00:18:20,835
- Oh my gosh!
- Yes! Tash is happy!

375
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:23,745
- Thank you so much, Elle, Mariposa!
- Sure!

376
00:18:23,879 --> 00:18:24,552
Can I…

377
00:18:24,577 --> 00:18:25,683
Oh, wait, wait, wait!

378
00:18:25,708 --> 00:18:27,062
- There!
- There!

379
00:18:27,133 --> 00:18:28,407
Wow!

380
00:18:29,126 --> 00:18:30,386
It’s so pretty!

381
00:18:32,723 --> 00:18:34,023
Oh my god!

382
00:18:37,755 --> 00:18:39,051
Thank you, guys!

383
00:18:39,143 --> 00:18:42,935
There were actually more choices,
but that was the best ex-deal—

384
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,129
just traded for some biscuits!

385
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:47,150
Thank you, thank you, Elle!

386
00:18:47,879 --> 00:18:48,505
- Why…
- Wait a sec…

387
00:18:48,530 --> 00:18:49,338
Why does it smell like chemicals?

388
00:18:49,363 --> 00:18:50,166
Yeah?

389
00:18:50,191 --> 00:18:51,269
Yeah!

390
00:18:51,331 --> 00:18:51,858
Yeah!

391
00:18:51,883 --> 00:18:52,462
Where did you get this, Cous?

392
00:18:52,487 --> 00:18:53,702
It smells like formalin!

393
00:18:54,421 --> 00:18:56,428
Wait. Elle, where did you get this?

394
00:18:56,823 --> 00:18:58,936
Come on! Where else?

395
00:18:59,242 --> 00:19:01,382
From Maligaya Funeral Home!

396
00:19:01,462 --> 00:19:02,215
- What?!
- What?!

397
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,581
That explains it!

398
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:06,127
Oh no, I remember now!

399
00:19:06,152 --> 00:19:08,313
This is what Aling Ebang
was wearing when she died!

400
00:19:08,338 --> 00:19:09,963
Her throat wart got infected!

401
00:19:13,962 --> 00:19:16,563
Kuya Aga, I did
everything I could to get

402
00:19:16,587 --> 00:19:19,645
ex-deals, but there’s
still something missing.

403
00:19:20,173 --> 00:19:23,273
So, for what’s missing,
we’ll have to pay for it?

404
00:19:23,417 --> 00:19:24,605
Yeah, pretty much.

405
00:19:25,145 --> 00:19:26,252
Here’s the list.

406
00:19:27,547 --> 00:19:30,006
Kuya, I’ll go ahead.
It’s getting dark.

407
00:19:30,304 --> 00:19:31,370
Okay, okay. Elle!

408
00:19:31,612 --> 00:19:32,636
Elle!

409
00:19:33,539 --> 00:19:34,347
Hmm?

410
00:19:34,492 --> 00:19:35,449
Oh!

411
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,527
God.

412
00:20:13,426 --> 00:20:15,233
- BFF!
- Hey, BFF!

413
00:20:16,145 --> 00:20:19,545
BFF, you look deep in thought.

414
00:20:19,795 --> 00:20:24,532
Why? Are you up to something
that Chacha doesn’t know about?

415
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,079
Oh, nothing. Me?

416
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:29,073
Maybe you're doing something she can’t see?

417
00:20:29,764 --> 00:20:30,671
Nothing.

418
00:20:30,890 --> 00:20:31,210
Nothing.

419
00:20:31,235 --> 00:20:32,674
Nothing, BFF. Come on, it’s me!

420
00:20:32,699 --> 00:20:33,752
Just making sure.

421
00:20:33,782 --> 00:20:35,222
I just wanted to ask you something.

422
00:20:35,635 --> 00:20:36,042
Oh no.

423
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:38,239
There’s something I’ve
really been meaning to ask.

424
00:20:38,264 --> 00:20:40,503
Wait… Are you about to
borrow money? No way!

425
00:20:40,528 --> 00:20:41,327
No, not that.

426
00:20:41,352 --> 00:20:41,820
Oh, okay.

427
00:20:42,091 --> 00:20:43,231
Okay, imagine this.

428
00:20:43,595 --> 00:20:44,549
You have a grandma.

429
00:20:45,505 --> 00:20:51,648
Now, she really wants
something, but you can’t afford it.

430
00:20:53,125 --> 00:20:56,451
Would you do whatever it
takes just to make her happy?

431
00:20:57,359 --> 00:20:58,663
- Me?
- Yeah?

432
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:00,358
Oh, I’d find a way.

433
00:21:00,499 --> 00:21:01,213
You’d find a way, huh?

434
00:21:01,238 --> 00:21:02,672
Of course! She’s my grandma!

435
00:21:02,795 --> 00:21:05,982
Even if it means using money
that was meant for something else…

436
00:21:06,007 --> 00:21:07,073
- Yeah, yeah, yeah…
- …you’d still use it?

437
00:21:07,098 --> 00:21:09,679
You’ve alloted the money for
something, but you’d still use it for her?

438
00:21:10,041 --> 00:21:12,221
Yeah! BFF, listen, I’ll tell you straight—

439
00:21:12,755 --> 00:21:16,488
I wouldn’t even be here if it
weren’t for my grandma. Right?

440
00:21:16,954 --> 00:21:22,917
You’ll meet a lot of people in life,
but you only have one grandma.

441
00:21:23,803 --> 00:21:26,736
We should love our grandmas.

442
00:21:28,142 --> 00:21:32,343
The love they give us is different.

443
00:21:33,432 --> 00:21:37,124
So if I were you, I’d do what I have to do.

444
00:21:39,055 --> 00:21:40,078
Hey!

445
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,103
I was wondering why you’re holding my hand!

446
00:21:43,278 --> 00:21:44,651
No, I was just thinking about my grandma!

447
00:21:45,316 --> 00:21:47,703
Got sentimental! I didn’t
mean anything by it.

448
00:21:47,789 --> 00:21:48,651
Okay, sorry.

449
00:21:48,676 --> 00:21:49,895
Do you get what I’m saying?

450
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,054
You’d find a way, right?

451
00:21:51,149 --> 00:21:52,129
I would.

452
00:21:52,154 --> 00:21:53,859
I don’t know about you
if you’re a bad grandkid.

453
00:21:54,052 --> 00:21:55,472
You’re right. You’re totally right.

454
00:21:56,612 --> 00:21:57,285
You’re totally right.

455
00:21:57,310 --> 00:21:58,943
Of course! Questions like these?

456
00:21:58,968 --> 00:22:00,849
- I can answer them in a snap.
- You’ve got a point.

457
00:22:00,995 --> 00:22:02,115
I know!

458
00:22:03,179 --> 00:22:04,233
Wait, wait, wait.

459
00:22:04,258 --> 00:22:05,238
What are you doing?

460
00:22:05,263 --> 00:22:06,429
Hold on.

461
00:22:06,693 --> 00:22:08,293
You're taking—wait!

462
00:22:08,351 --> 00:22:09,435
Hey, this is Tso K’s money!

463
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:10,159
Hold on, hold on!

464
00:22:10,184 --> 00:22:11,769
But—wait! Are you really
gonna pay me with that?

465
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,913
Why are you taking some?! What’s it for?!

466
00:22:13,938 --> 00:22:16,761
This is for what I couldn’t
get in the ex-deals.

467
00:22:17,249 --> 00:22:18,923
I’ll use this first.

468
00:22:19,409 --> 00:22:19,816
Why?!

469
00:22:19,846 --> 00:22:21,088
So I’m taking a bit.

470
00:22:21,828 --> 00:22:23,261
You said you wouldn’t borrow money!

471
00:22:23,388 --> 00:22:24,395
Did I already pay you?

472
00:22:24,628 --> 00:22:25,480
No.

473
00:22:25,505 --> 00:22:27,046
Then I didn’t borrow anything!

474
00:22:27,071 --> 00:22:28,465
I just deducted some.

475
00:22:28,768 --> 00:22:30,288
And now, I’m
paying you with this.

476
00:22:30,768 --> 00:22:31,650
Here.

477
00:22:31,675 --> 00:22:33,518
I didn’t borrow
anything from you.

478
00:22:33,588 --> 00:22:34,110
But—!

479
00:22:34,135 --> 00:22:35,389
I need to use it first.

480
00:22:35,414 --> 00:22:36,790
You said it yourself, for Grandma.

481
00:22:36,857 --> 00:22:40,143
- But—! That’s not enough anymore!
- You said it

482
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:42,367
Lola Maxi, it smells amazing!
Kuya Aga, it smells so good!

483
00:22:42,392 --> 00:22:45,158
But your cooking is taking forever!

484
00:22:45,202 --> 00:22:45,788
It’s almost done!

485
00:22:45,813 --> 00:22:47,361
- That’s just the sauce!
- It’s already 7 PM!

486
00:22:47,516 --> 00:22:49,623
- I’ll go get the cheese!
- The Pers Family is starving!

487
00:22:49,673 --> 00:22:51,320
Lola Maxi, you’re getting the cheese?

488
00:22:51,345 --> 00:22:52,756
- Yes! I’ll get it, I’ll get it.
- Okay, thank you!

489
00:22:52,781 --> 00:22:54,048
It’s done!

490
00:22:55,398 --> 00:22:58,077
Is it still going to take long?
Here it is! Here it is!

491
00:22:59,188 --> 00:23:00,255
Smells delicious!

492
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:05,031
I should serve my birthday girl first, but
since you’re all impatient, you go ahead!

493
00:23:05,099 --> 00:23:09,653
Come on, you started cooking that
sauce at 5 PM, and now it’s almost 7!

494
00:23:11,016 --> 00:23:11,683
Is it good to go?

495
00:23:11,708 --> 00:23:12,956
- It’s good to go!
- Yeah, it’s good to go!

496
00:23:13,913 --> 00:23:14,926
- Hey!
- Whoa!

497
00:23:14,964 --> 00:23:16,270
So good!

498
00:23:16,295 --> 00:23:21,145
Tasha, sorry, you were supposed
to be first, but… but here, for my love.

499
00:23:21,170 --> 00:23:23,645
- No problem.
- Alright, let’s hurry, let’s hurry!

500
00:23:26,107 --> 00:23:27,224
Hey!

501
00:23:30,467 --> 00:23:32,187
- Kuya…
- Oh no!

502
00:23:35,178 --> 00:23:36,498
- Oh no!
- Kuya!

503
00:23:37,859 --> 00:23:39,313
I got the cheese!

504
00:23:43,378 --> 00:23:44,463
What’s wrong?

505
00:23:44,626 --> 00:23:45,666
- Uh…
- Why are you all so quiet?

506
00:23:45,691 --> 00:23:46,993
- Uh…
- Mmmm…

507
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,414
Ah!

508
00:23:51,524 --> 00:23:54,084
Huh?! What happened?!

509
00:23:55,150 --> 00:23:55,971
Huh?!

510
00:23:55,996 --> 00:23:57,516
What happened to the gown?!

511
00:23:57,582 --> 00:23:58,882
Lo…Lola Maxi, so…

512
00:23:59,583 --> 00:24:05,713
I was serving the sauce, then
I tripped… And it landed there.

513
00:24:05,738 --> 00:24:06,846
I got some on me too…

514
00:24:07,877 --> 00:24:11,163
I knew it! You never really
wanted this debut to happen!

515
00:24:11,611 --> 00:24:15,451
Lola Maxi, it was an
accident. He didn’t mean to.

516
00:24:16,338 --> 00:24:19,158
You know what, I’m sorry
for pushing this so much.

517
00:24:20,369 --> 00:24:22,055
Are you happy now? You won?

518
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:25,513
Lola Maxi…

519
00:24:25,538 --> 00:24:29,218
- Lola Maxi, it was really Iskineport…
- Hey, me?! Kuya…

520
00:24:29,454 --> 00:24:32,994
Do you know why I really
want this debut to happen?

521
00:24:37,123 --> 00:24:43,736
Because I was one of those kids
who dreamed of wearing a gown

522
00:24:45,063 --> 00:24:47,743
and being danced by my loved ones.

523
00:24:48,971 --> 00:24:50,851
Every year, I wished for it.

524
00:24:53,172 --> 00:24:55,565
But they always said there was no money.

525
00:24:56,298 --> 00:25:02,132
Until my father passed away,
and I never got to reach that dream.

526
00:25:05,662 --> 00:25:07,248
I started working early.

527
00:25:08,770 --> 00:25:10,503
I became the breadwinner.

528
00:25:12,090 --> 00:25:14,357
I dedicated my life to...

529
00:25:15,390 --> 00:25:17,703
helping my loved ones.

530
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:22,793
But I forgot to help myself...

531
00:25:23,372 --> 00:25:25,112
to achieve my own dream.

532
00:25:28,692 --> 00:25:35,413
People say that a debut is just a
luxury, but why do we work so hard?

533
00:25:37,145 --> 00:25:38,812
Isn’t it to be happy?

534
00:25:40,718 --> 00:25:41,725
Lola Maxi,

535
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:50,222
first of all, I just want to apologize
if we, or I, were a bit insensitive.

536
00:25:51,910 --> 00:25:55,463
But you were right, weren’t you? Um…

537
00:25:56,970 --> 00:25:59,070
all I really want to say is...

538
00:25:59,785 --> 00:26:03,338
what’s the point of
earning all this money,

539
00:26:04,055 --> 00:26:05,562
or having all these things,

540
00:26:06,048 --> 00:26:07,448
if you can’t even do

541
00:26:08,416 --> 00:26:11,029
the one thing that
truly makes you happy?

542
00:26:12,615 --> 00:26:16,692
And, sorry, Lola Maxi,
that we didn’t understand

543
00:26:16,716 --> 00:26:20,531
right away what you
were trying to tell us.

544
00:26:21,188 --> 00:26:23,948
But I just want
to say, Lola Maxi,

545
00:26:24,932 --> 00:26:26,305
that we love you so much.

546
00:26:27,910 --> 00:26:29,964
- We love you!
- We love you, Lola Maxi!

547
00:26:30,281 --> 00:26:31,448
I love you, too!

548
00:26:38,968 --> 00:26:40,061
Happy birthday!

549
00:26:40,996 --> 00:26:42,503
Thank you, Lola! I love you!

550
00:26:44,537 --> 00:26:47,350
Hey, Lola Maxi, don’t worry.

551
00:26:48,888 --> 00:26:53,042
They say promises are
meant to be broken, but I swear,

552
00:26:53,618 --> 00:26:56,785
I’ll make sure this debut happens.

553
00:26:57,895 --> 00:26:58,795
Really, my love?

554
00:26:58,820 --> 00:26:59,676
Of course.

555
00:27:00,774 --> 00:27:07,157
You know, who else is going to support and
stand by each other through thick and thin?

556
00:27:08,235 --> 00:27:09,188
Us!

557
00:27:09,804 --> 00:27:10,938
It’s us.

558
00:27:11,705 --> 00:27:12,766
Right?

559
00:27:15,428 --> 00:27:16,961
Love you, Lola Maxi!

560
00:27:17,465 --> 00:27:18,752
- Love you, Tash!
- Love you!

561
00:27:18,915 --> 00:27:21,175
- Love you, ‘Dres!
- Love you, guys!

562
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:22,348
Love you, guys!

563
00:27:22,563 --> 00:27:25,250
Happy birthday to you!

564
00:27:25,606 --> 00:27:30,120
Happy birthday, happy birthday!

565
00:27:30,658 --> 00:27:36,458
Happy birthday to you!

566
00:27:38,805 --> 00:27:40,078
Make a wish, make a wish!

567
00:27:46,650 --> 00:27:50,084
Now, my wish for you,
my daughter, is simple.

568
00:27:50,109 --> 00:27:51,744
I’m just so happy for you.

569
00:27:52,037 --> 00:27:55,123
I’m sorry that you never got
to have your debut before…

570
00:27:55,525 --> 00:27:57,218
we just couldn’t
afford it back then.

571
00:27:57,877 --> 00:28:01,490
But we did everything we
could to make this happen now.

572
00:28:01,515 --> 00:28:03,043
So, happy, happy birthday to you.

573
00:28:03,459 --> 00:28:13,128
And I hope that one day… one day,
you’ll find a man who will truly love you.

574
00:28:13,293 --> 00:28:16,747
Whatever brings you
happiness in this world,

575
00:28:16,771 --> 00:28:20,226
that’s what will truly
make me happy, too.

576
00:28:20,258 --> 00:28:21,864
I love you so much, Tasha.

577
00:28:23,652 --> 00:28:31,495
From then, until now, and for the rest of
your life, I will always be here for you.

578
00:28:31,520 --> 00:28:34,536
Awwwww. Thank you!

579
00:28:34,709 --> 00:28:35,815
Happy birthday to you too, Andres!

580
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:37,213
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

581
00:28:37,361 --> 00:28:39,668
And of course, happy birthday, Tash!

582
00:28:39,693 --> 00:28:46,207
I know you and Andres both sacrificed
a lot just to help with our bakery.

583
00:28:46,756 --> 00:28:50,168
I just want you to know that
we appreciate you both so much.

584
00:28:50,255 --> 00:28:51,609
We are so proud of you.

585
00:28:51,634 --> 00:28:53,917
- Thank you!
- Happy birthday!

586
00:28:53,942 --> 00:28:55,389
- Thank you!
- Thank you, guys!

587
00:28:55,414 --> 00:28:57,267
Charlene’s really great with words, huh?

588
00:28:59,503 --> 00:29:04,729
Guys, I just wanted to say thank you to
everyone who helped make my debut happen.

589
00:29:05,293 --> 00:29:09,046
Especially my parents.
I wanna thank Tso K…

590
00:29:09,071 --> 00:29:09,477
Yeah…

591
00:29:09,507 --> 00:29:13,487
Tito Iskineport, Boss Beauty, Mariposa,

592
00:29:13,896 --> 00:29:17,522
Anne, Kuya Chard, Ate
Elle, and most especially,

593
00:29:17,994 --> 00:29:22,632
my brother, who gave up his own
birthday just to make this happen.

594
00:29:22,657 --> 00:29:26,205
- Yes! Wow!
- Love you!

595
00:29:26,789 --> 00:29:28,076
Thank you!

596
00:29:28,101 --> 00:29:30,671
- Wow.
- Yehey!

597
00:29:32,545 --> 00:29:33,845
- Here comes Lola Maxi!
- Oh!

598
00:29:33,870 --> 00:29:36,358
- Where am I—
- Just trust me!

599
00:29:36,515 --> 00:29:38,282
Right, right, right!

600
00:29:38,307 --> 00:29:40,043
Where are you taking me?

601
00:29:40,068 --> 00:29:41,374
Oh, just keep going straight!

602
00:29:41,820 --> 00:29:42,773
Slowly!

603
00:29:42,798 --> 00:29:44,682
This is kind of scary!

604
00:29:44,707 --> 00:29:45,948
We’re almost there!

605
00:29:45,973 --> 00:29:46,799
Just a little more!

606
00:29:46,824 --> 00:29:49,474
If you’re messing with me—!

607
00:29:49,499 --> 00:29:50,793
I’m not! We’re here!

608
00:29:50,818 --> 00:29:52,897
Stop, stop, stop!

609
00:29:52,957 --> 00:29:54,123
- This is it!
- Where are we?

610
00:29:54,196 --> 00:29:55,676
Open your eyes!

611
00:29:56,009 --> 00:29:59,009
Surprise!

612
00:29:59,248 --> 00:30:01,208
Wow!

613
00:30:01,233 --> 00:30:04,383
Oh wow! Everything looks so beautiful!

614
00:30:06,097 --> 00:30:07,910
Guys, I have a speech too.

615
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:14,448
I want to dedicate this debut party to
the most important person in our home.

616
00:30:14,917 --> 00:30:15,717
Tash…

617
00:30:16,518 --> 00:30:20,345
The person who never gets
tired of teaching us values—

618
00:30:20,839 --> 00:30:23,506
our very own Lola, Lola Maxi!

619
00:30:27,071 --> 00:30:29,644
Thank you so much,
Lola Maxi, for everything!

620
00:30:29,669 --> 00:30:30,864
We love you!

621
00:30:30,889 --> 00:30:32,870
We love you so much!

622
00:30:34,593 --> 00:30:35,227
Music!

623
00:30:39,176 --> 00:30:40,763
Party time!

624
00:30:41,943 --> 00:30:42,603
Thank you!

625
00:30:44,253 --> 00:30:45,346
For me?!

626
00:30:45,639 --> 00:30:46,959
Yes!

627
00:30:47,323 --> 00:30:49,456
Awwww!

628
00:31:01,214 --> 00:31:03,168
This is beautiful!

629
00:31:13,318 --> 00:31:14,584
Yes, Lola Maxi!

630
00:32:00,526 --> 00:32:02,039
I spent my own money for this!

631
00:32:06,035 --> 00:32:07,135
Look, look at Lola Maxi.

632
00:32:07,748 --> 00:32:09,614
She looks like
she’s floating on air!

633
00:32:09,822 --> 00:32:13,995
Of course! Her dream of having a
debut finally came true, didn’t it?!

634
00:32:14,601 --> 00:32:16,961
And I’m so proud of all of you!

635
00:32:18,993 --> 00:32:22,240
And you know, Lola Maxi is right—

636
00:32:23,301 --> 00:32:27,873
what’s the point of money
if you’re not happy in life?

637
00:32:28,615 --> 00:32:30,121
Then just give it to me and Chard!

638
00:32:30,154 --> 00:32:31,588
Yeah! We’ll be the happy ones!

639
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:34,947
There’s no money left!
We barely had enough!

640
00:32:35,228 --> 00:32:36,348
Then let’s just forgive and forget!

641
00:32:37,315 --> 00:32:39,921
- Elle! Elle, Elle!
- Hey!

642
00:32:40,245 --> 00:32:40,685
Yes?

643
00:32:40,958 --> 00:32:42,545
I just wanted to say goodbye.

644
00:32:42,767 --> 00:32:43,813
Of course!

645
00:32:44,373 --> 00:32:46,807
Thank you so, so much. Really,
thank you, thank you, thank you!

646
00:32:46,832 --> 00:32:47,730
Thank you!

647
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:49,449
Sit down.

648
00:32:49,474 --> 00:32:50,480
Here.

649
00:32:50,990 --> 00:32:54,517
You can say thank you without holding
on to someone or standing up, right?

650
00:32:54,723 --> 00:32:55,725
Yeah, that’s true!

651
00:32:55,750 --> 00:32:56,777
Thank you, okay?

652
00:32:57,391 --> 00:32:59,637
Thank you, thank you,
Elle. Thank you so much!

653
00:32:59,662 --> 00:33:01,221
Thank you, Ate Elle.

654
00:33:01,246 --> 00:33:05,756
Thank you so much, even if we
only had a small budget for this debut.

655
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:06,807
Oh, see?

656
00:33:06,832 --> 00:33:08,710
Thank you so much.

657
00:33:08,735 --> 00:33:12,203
That’s how you do it! See? You
can say thanks while sitting down!

658
00:33:12,562 --> 00:33:13,697
It’s easy, right?!

659
00:33:13,722 --> 00:33:16,968
Uh, Ate Elle, thank you. Thank you, too.

660
00:33:16,993 --> 00:33:19,143
Wait—why is he standing up?

661
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:21,013
He doesn’t have a wife, does he?

662
00:33:21,561 --> 00:33:25,388
If you don’t have a wife, you can stand.
If you do, you should sit. Thank you, Elle!

663
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:27,127
- Do you have a wife?
- I do!

664
00:33:27,229 --> 00:33:27,857
And I don’t?

665
00:33:27,882 --> 00:33:30,649
Well, you kind of look like you’re
sitting, even though you’re standing.

666
00:33:30,674 --> 00:33:32,521
Anyway, thank you, Elle!
Thanks, thanks, thanks!

667
00:33:32,546 --> 00:33:35,725
No problem, as long as
you don’t forget our deal!

668
00:33:35,790 --> 00:33:38,024
- Ey!
- Ey!

669
00:33:40,873 --> 00:33:42,793
Orb, is this taking much longer?

670
00:33:42,889 --> 00:33:43,920
What’s going on?

671
00:33:44,086 --> 00:33:45,879
Just a second, Orb, okay?

672
00:33:46,312 --> 00:33:47,914
Just a moment… Just a little more.

673
00:33:47,939 --> 00:33:49,021
Okay.

674
00:33:50,071 --> 00:33:52,598
Two…one…

675
00:33:52,623 --> 00:33:55,055
- It’s ready, Orb! Take it off!
- Is it time? Is it ready?

676
00:33:55,651 --> 00:33:59,198
Surprise! Happy birthday, Orb!

677
00:34:00,386 --> 00:34:02,639
Sorry, this is
all I could afford.

678
00:34:02,998 --> 00:34:05,505
Wow, you got me a gift?!

679
00:34:05,606 --> 00:34:08,833
I had so many expenses!
And I even bought a gi—

680
00:34:10,627 --> 00:34:13,000
Wow! Thank you!

681
00:34:13,262 --> 00:34:14,293
Thank you…

682
00:34:16,501 --> 00:34:18,081
Wow!

683
00:34:18,658 --> 00:34:19,751
This is amazing!

684
00:34:20,209 --> 00:34:20,815
It really is.

685
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:22,275
Did you use my money to buy this?

686
00:34:23,355 --> 00:34:25,394
Oh! You're here Tso K.

687
00:34:25,614 --> 00:34:26,354
You guys!

688
00:34:26,379 --> 00:34:31,977
Happy birthday to you!

689
00:34:32,498 --> 00:34:42,151
Happy birthday to you,
happy birthday to you!

690
00:34:44,805 --> 00:34:45,819
Thank you, guys!

691
00:34:45,844 --> 00:34:46,851
Wish!

692
00:34:47,787 --> 00:34:51,739
I think I know your wish…
and I think it already came true.

693
00:34:54,693 --> 00:34:57,060
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

694
00:34:57,085 --> 00:34:58,473
Thank you, guys!

695
00:34:58,498 --> 00:35:00,526
You thought we forgot, huh?

696
00:35:00,891 --> 00:35:02,718
I really did… I thought you guys forgot.

697
00:35:02,792 --> 00:35:04,072
But thank you!

698
00:35:04,183 --> 00:35:08,543
This is really… my most
memorable birthday ever.

699
00:35:08,637 --> 00:35:10,057
- Mmm…
- Awww…

700
00:35:10,082 --> 00:35:12,631
So much has happened,
and I’ve learned a lot too.

701
00:35:12,897 --> 00:35:14,397
So, thank you, guys!

702
00:35:14,877 --> 00:35:16,377
Why is he looking at you like that?

703
00:35:19,062 --> 00:35:22,715
Oh wow! Kuya’s blushing!

704
00:35:24,076 --> 00:35:29,882
Anyway, that’s why Mom, Dad,
and Lola’s motto is always right.

705
00:35:30,508 --> 00:35:31,761
Let’s all say it together…

706
00:35:31,786 --> 00:35:34,113
But wait, wait, wait!
What’s your wish first?

707
00:35:34,413 --> 00:35:34,915
Me?

708
00:35:34,940 --> 00:35:37,369
It’s okay. You already know what it is.

709
00:35:39,949 --> 00:35:41,882
I know his wish!

710
00:35:41,914 --> 00:35:44,413
I’ll say Andres’
and Atasha’s wish…

711
00:35:44,438 --> 00:35:45,897
Oh no…

712
00:35:46,094 --> 00:35:46,867
Don’t, Dad!

713
00:35:48,511 --> 00:35:49,538
Like they say…

714
00:35:50,316 --> 00:35:56,603
Through problems and happiness,
Pers is first, Pers is the hero!
